From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: seg6: forward L3 lwtunnel modes through ip_forward/ip6_forward

RFC 8986 Section 5.1 (H.Encaps) requires:

  "S05.   Decrement inner IPv6 Hop Limit or IPv4 TTL"
  "The received packet is encapsulated unmodified (with the exception of
  the IPv4 TTL or IPv6 Hop Limit that is decremented as described in
  [RFC2473])."

RFC 2473 Section 3.1 ties the decrement to forwarding, so locally
originated packets owe no decrement while forwarded packets must have
their inner IPv4 TTL or IPv6 Hop Limit checked and decremented before
encapsulation.

Today seg6_build_state() sets LWTUNNEL_STATE_INPUT_REDIRECT for every
mode, which bypasses ip_forward()/ip6_forward() and sends forwarded
packets directly to seg6_input_core(). Nothing checks or decrements the
inner TTL or Hop Limit; packets arriving with TTL or Hop Limit 1 are
encapsulated and forwarded, and the comment in __seg6_do_srh_encap()
claiming decapsulation overwrites the inner Hop Limit with the outer
Hop Limit is false (seg6_local.c has no hop-limit copy).

Follow the MPLS lwtunnel precedent (mpls_build_state() sets only
LWTUNNEL_STATE_XMIT_REDIRECT): keep LWTUNNEL_STATE_INPUT_REDIRECT for
the L2 modes (l2encap, l2encap.red, which carry Ethernet frames with no
IP TTL) and set only LWTUNNEL_STATE_OUTPUT_REDIRECT for the L3 modes
(encap, encap.red, inline). Forwarded L3 packets then traverse
ip_forward()/ip6_forward() before reaching lwtunnel_output() and
seg6_output_core(), giving one decrement and ICMP Time Exceeded to the
sender on expiry while leaving locally originated traffic unchanged.

Forward-path consequences:
- The first-SID lookup moves from ip6_route_input() (which uses the
  ingress interface) to ip6_route_output() (output routing without iif).
- The FORWARD netfilter hook and XFRM forward policy now see the inner
  packet before encapsulation.
- ip_dst_mtu_maybe_forward() and ip6_dst_mtu_maybe_forward() subtract
  lwtunnel_headroom(), so oversized DF-set IPv4 or IPv6 packets now
  signal PMTU (Fragmentation Needed / Packet Too Big) minus headroom to
  the sender.

CONFIG_IPV6_SEG6_FORWARD_TTL identifies this capability to the runtime
kernel manifest; it has no alternate datapath or disable switch.

Based on Linux v7.3.

--- a/net/ipv6/Kconfig
+++ b/net/ipv6/Kconfig
@@ -296,6 +296,10 @@
 	  processing of SRv6 packets based on their active segment.
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
+
+config IPV6_SEG6_FORWARD_TTL
+	def_bool y
+	depends on IPV6_SEG6_LWTUNNEL
 
 config IPV6_SEG6_HMAC
 	bool "IPv6: Segment Routing HMAC support"
--- a/net/ipv6/seg6_iptunnel.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/seg6_iptunnel.c
@@ -165,10 +165,12 @@
 	skb_mac_header_rebuild(skb);
 	hdr = ipv6_hdr(skb);
 
-	/* inherit tc, flowlabel and hlim
-	 * hlim will be decremented in ip6_forward() afterwards and
-	 * decapsulation will overwrite inner hlim with outer hlim
-	 */
+	/* Inherit tc, flowlabel and hlim for IPv6 inner packets. Forwarded L3
+	 * packets reach seg6_output_core() via ip_forward()/ip6_forward(),
+	 * which already checked and decremented the inner TTL or Hop Limit
+	 * (RFC 8986 Section 5.1 S05); locally originated packets owe no
+	 * decrement (RFC 2473 Section 3.1).
+	 */
 
 	if (skb->protocol == htons(ETH_P_IPV6)) {
 		ip6_flow_hdr(hdr, ip6_tclass(ip6_flowinfo(inner_hdr)),
@@ -843,12 +845,18 @@
 	}
 
 	newts->type = LWTUNNEL_ENCAP_SEG6;
-	newts->flags |= LWTUNNEL_STATE_INPUT_REDIRECT;
 
-	if (tuninfo->mode != SEG6_IPTUN_MODE_L2ENCAP &&
-	    tuninfo->mode != SEG6_IPTUN_MODE_L2ENCAP_RED)
-		newts->flags |= LWTUNNEL_STATE_OUTPUT_REDIRECT;
+	/* Forwarded L3 packets must traverse ip_forward()/ip6_forward() so
+	 * the inner TTL or Hop Limit is checked and decremented once before
+	 * encapsulation (RFC 8986 Section 5.1 S05); L2 modes carry Ethernet
+	 * frames with no IP TTL and keep input redirect.
+	 */
+	if (tuninfo->mode == SEG6_IPTUN_MODE_L2ENCAP ||
+	    tuninfo->mode == SEG6_IPTUN_MODE_L2ENCAP_RED)
+		newts->flags |= LWTUNNEL_STATE_INPUT_REDIRECT;
+	else
+		newts->flags |= LWTUNNEL_STATE_OUTPUT_REDIRECT;
 
 	newts->headroom = seg6_lwt_headroom(tuninfo);
 
 	*ts = newts;
